{% comment %}
  Ron's Pijamas – decides which Size Guide (metaobject type `size_guide`) a
  product uses and outputs that entry's handle, or nothing.

  Rules, in order:
  1. Product metafield custom.hide_size_guide is true → no guide.
  2. Product metafield custom.size_guide (Metaobject reference → Size Guides)
     → that entry.
  3. Otherwise the store default: the first Size Guides entry whose
     "Основна таблица" (is_default) field is ticked.
  A guide is only used when it has at least one size, so no table is ever
  shown without real measurements. All data comes from Shopify Admin
  (Content › Metaobjects); nothing is hardcoded here.

  Liquid snippets can't return objects, so callers capture the handle and
  look the entry up:
    {%- capture guide_handle -%}{% render 'rons-size-guide-resolve', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign guide = shop.metaobjects.size_guide[guide_handle] -%}

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  unless product.metafields.custom.hide_size_guide.value == true
    assign guide = null
    assign product_guide = product.metafields.custom.size_guide
    if product_guide.type == 'metaobject_reference' and product_guide.value != blank
      assign guide = product_guide.value
    else
      for entry in shop.metaobjects.size_guide.values
        if entry.is_default.value == true
          assign guide = entry
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif

    if guide != blank and guide.sizes.value.size > 0
      echo guide.system.handle
    endif
  endunless
-%}
